<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="PHM" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Philemon</para>
  <para style="mt">Philemon</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char>, a prisoner of Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char> Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char>, and Timothy <char style="add">[honoring God] [our]</char> brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And to <char style="add">[our]</char> beloved Apphia <char style="add">[fruitful]</char>, and Archippus <char style="add">[master of the horse]</char> our fellowsoldier, and to the church in your<char style="ord">i</char> house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Grace to you, and peace, from God-The Father our Father and the Lord - Kurios <char style="add">[he to whom a person belongs]</char> Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char> Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />I thank my God-The Father, making mention of you<char style="ord">i</char> always in my prayers,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Hearing of your<char style="ord">i</char> love and faith, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have toward the Lord - Kurios <char style="add">[he to whom a person belongs]</char> Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char>, and toward all saints;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />That the communication of your<char style="ord">i</char> faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char> Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For we have great joy and consolation in your<char style="ord">i</char> love, because the bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> of the saints are refreshed by your<char style="ord">i</char>, brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For what reason, though I might be much bold in Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char> to command <char style="pn">(charge)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> that which is convenient <char style="pn">(fit; appropriate; proper (one’s own; peculiar; particular))</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>, being such an one as Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> the aged, and now also a prisoner of Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char> Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> for my son Onesimus <char style="add">[profitable or useful]</char>, whom I have begotten in my bonds:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Which in time past was to you<char style="ord">i</char> unprofitable, but now profitable to you<char style="ord">i</char> and to me:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Whom I have sent again: you<char style="ord">i</char> therefore receive him, that is, my own bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Whom I would have retained with me, that in your<char style="ord">i</char> stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the Gospel <char style="pn">(joyful message)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But without your<char style="ord">i</char> mind would I do nothing; that your<char style="ord">i</char> benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should receive him forever;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Not now as a slave, but above a slave, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, both in the flesh, and in the Lord - Kurios?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />If he has wronged you<char style="ord">i</char>, or owes <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> ought, put that on my account;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />I Sha’ul <char style="add">[desired]</char> have written <char style="add">[it]</char> with my own hand, I will repay <char style="add">[it]</char>: albeit I do not say to you<char style="ord">i</char> how you<char style="ord">i</char> owe unto me even your<char style="ord">i</char> own self besides.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Yes, brother, let me have joy of you<char style="ord">i</char> in the Lord - Kurios: refresh my bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> in the Lord - Kurios.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Having confidence in your<char style="ord">i</char> obedience I wrote unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, knowing that you<char style="ord">i</char> will also do more than I say.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />There salute you<char style="ord">i</char> Epaphras <char style="add">[lovely]</char>, my fellowprisoner in Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah]</char> Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Marcus <char style="add">[a defense]</char>, Aristarchus <char style="add">[the best ruler]</char>, Demas <char style="add">[governor of the people]</char>, Lucas <char style="add">[light-giving]</char>, my fellowlabourers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />The grace of our Lord - Kurios <char style="add">[he to whom a person belongs]</char> Yeshua <char style="add">[God is Salvation]</char> Moshiach <char style="add">[Messiah] [be]</char> with your Spirit <char style="add">[Ruach]</char>. Amen. &lt;[Written from Rome <char style="add">[strength]</char> to Philemon, by Onesimus <char style="add">[profitable or useful]</char> a slave.]&gt;</para>
</usx>